I have to say that I own both Golf It! and Golf with your friends, so here's a little comparison between
and
:
➜ The power that you hit the ball is measured by the movement of your mouse, which means that you have more control over the power that you put on the ball, also means that the shots become more skillfull rather than with a power bar like Gof with your friends;
➜ It has workshop and a level editor, which means it has loads of different levels to try and create;
➜ The physics are great.
➜ Ball customization is alright, it doesn't have loads of different customs but probably they will keep adding some.
➜ The lack of more mods that you can put into the game, like different shapes, ball jump and many other aspects that Golf with your friends has for example;
➜ The loading screen is quite annoying, it takes so long to load into the game when you open it (although I have to say that when you start a match there's almost no loading time), I decided to put in the cons because it could be improved.
➜ It has loads of in-game mods that you can add to each match to make it way more fun;
➜ The physics are quite good, but not better than Golf It!;
➜ Ball customization is great, it has different colours of trails and loads of hats.
➜ It does not have workshop, which is a shame for the developers for such a good game like Golf with your friends;
➜ Lack of new maps, caused by not having workshop!
Don't get me wrong, both games are so much fun and they are really great games. I am just trying to help those who are in doubt between those two games. I would get both if possible, because some features lack on each game.
🎮7.5/10 on both games🎮

Short description:
A surprising underdog!
Pros:
- It is a free game that does not try to extort money from you and it is well made and complete!!! How often do you find one of these?! SERIOUSLY??!?!?!?!
- Combat system feels great and adequate to this game;
- Elaborated dialogues;
- Immersive environments;
- Features a culture rich world (mostly Nordic);
- Memorable characters;
- Fully voiced;
- Re-playability through the different classes your character may assume;
- Challenging.
Cons:
- Graphics may not please all audiences;
- Walking through the map takes a lot of time (although you can speed up the game in the options menu);
- The menus could be a little easier to access (but you can have hot-keys in your keyboard in order);
- The initial quest in the game (where you must gather food) may be a little hard for people not used to this type of game;
Long description:
I must say that this game surprised me.
At first, I was reluctant to play it, because it seemed to resolve around a combat system, and I just wanted a good-old-fashioned point'n click adventure.
However, this game won me in the first few minutes, when the first dialogue came up fully voiced, presenting a memorable character (Thrivaldi, you arr awesome!).
As for my concerns with the combat system, well... I was wrong. The game heavily resolves around pointing and clicking on the environment, and the combat system is actually FUN. It is not rare to find myself wandering the woods, looking for random encounters, so that I can play the combat mini game once more.
The puzzles are challenging and fair. You will feel accomplished by completing them without relying to online sources.
Although not all dialogue lines are interesting, they help to add this sense of immersion to the game.
The game has it's flaws, though...
Walking through the forest may be a pain... Without a warp system, you will spend a lot of time travelling from point A to B, sometimes, only to TRY to gather an item. Repeating this journey will prove to be very time consuming.
The auto save feature is nice; but it would be even nicer if they added a "before dying" or "before entering a dangerous area" save, since it is something that will be happening a lot to your character.
The menus try to be simple, but having sub-menus consumes more time in order to do a task. The game offers hot-keys to these actions though, so I recommend learning and using them.
Final words:
So, all in all, this game proved to be a great gaming experience for me. I highly recommend it!

